-- Generated from the cMaNGOS classic world DB and Forever's zone maps; do not edit by hand.
-- Data fixes are welcome as a PR or a data-error issue.
-- Herb and ore positions in Forever's new zones (Zephras Isle, Riverglades, Shen'dralas)
-- come from GatherLite (MIT, Copyright (c) 2019 Wuild), which takes them from Wowhead.
-- See LICENSE.txt.
-- i<entry>: skinning loot ItemTree's players recorded in Forever (ItemTree 1.2.8,
--   data build 1.60.1.71037) for a creature the classic database gives none. An item's chance is
--   its share of the creature's recorded skins.
-- Data: ForeverDB.net (https://foreverdb.net), build 1.60.1.71037. Reuse requires this credit: see LICENSE.txt (GPL-3.0 section 7(b)).
-- Points players saw in Forever (zones whose data lacked a kind) come from ForeverDB.
-- x393: a skinnable creature only ForeverDB knows; its loot is in no input.
-- water: open-water points players fished in Forever. Not read: no input has the zone's fishing
--        level or catch.
-- loot:  key -> { { item, chance %, average count }, ... }
-- mobs:  entry -> { name, minLevel, maxLevel, { [skillLine] = lootKey } }
-- nodes: entry -> { name, skill (nil for fishing pools), lootKey, skillLine }
-- zones: uiMapID -> { map = continent, w, h = size in yards, lvl = { low, high },
--                     mobs = { [entry] = clusters }, nodes = same,
--                     fish = { base = zone fishing level, loot = lootKey },
--                     mix = { { clusters, { [entry] = percent, ... }, how }, ... } }
--        mix: spawn points that hold one of several kinds, each kind by its share; the same clusters
--             sit in each kind's nodes. how: "db" the classic database's odds, "like" GatherLite's
--             shared spot with the classic odds of the same kinds, "even" an even split (no odds known)
--        100000 + map id -> the same for an instance, with inst = map id (no game map)
--        cloth = { [item] = { { need, lo, hi, kills, perKill, spots, about, type, who? }, ... } }: the
--             zone's cloth droppers in bands of 5 levels (need: the band's highest minimum level; lo, hi:
--             its level span; kills: spawns; perKill: cloth a kill; spots: up to 3 clusters; about: each
--             spot's { lead creature, low, high level }; type: CreatureType; who: "A" or "H" when only
--             that faction may kill them).
-- clusters: 5 characters each, base-92 digits (ASCII 33-126 without the double quote and backslash):
--   x (2 digits), y (2 digits) on the zone map out of 92*92-1, then the spawn count.
-- fishing: ranks = { { skill, kind, npcs, item?, quest?, level?, at? } } (level: player level to learn it,
--          at: Fishing skill it's learnable from), npcs = { [entry] = { name, side, spawns } }
-- ranks: skillLine -> { { skill = cap it lifts, level = player level, npcs } } for Herbalism, Mining,
--        Skinning; rankNpcs: [entry] = { name, side, spawns }
-- packed: loot, mobs and zones ship as one table constructor string per key, decoded on first
--         read (the code at the end). A zone keeps map, w, h, lvl, inst and fish plain, plus
--         has = " m<entry> ... n<entry> ", the creatures and nodes it holds.
-- index: flat lists the addon's whole-table loops read instead of decoding every entry:
--        looted = every looted item; skins = entry, name, minLevel, maxLevel, skinning lootKey;
--        farm = item, entry, skillLine, chance %, minLevel of each creature loot row.

